      "review",
      "accepted",
      "rejected",
      "shipped",
      "abandoned"
    ],
    "note": "The scheduler vocabulary is CONFIGURED, never a hard-coded constant list. The workspace catalog carries ten tokens; the registry configures four; terminal-success is the two-token actual lifecycle {done, archived}. Every catalog token outside executable + terminal_success is unsupported and halts. archived satisfies a DEPENDENCY but does NOT close a green-maker obligation, because it may be a descope."
